post the recipe for it one of these days. It&#39;s a&nbsp;seeded&nbsp;sourdough sandwich bread that I make with just a touch of yeast so that I can make it in&nbsp;about 3 1/2 hours without an overnight ferment.&nbsp;</span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">It&#39;s perfect for this crunchy, hearty grilled sandwich. It adds&nbsp;a&nbsp;tangy flavor that really enhances the Hatch chili&nbsp;and smoky bacon.</span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></h5>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-lo1v07rm":{"meshProps":{"wedges":[],"rotatedComponents":[],"fixedComponents":[]},"fillLayers":{"containerId":"comp-lo1v07rm","hasBgFullscreenScrollEffect":false,"shouldRenderUnderlay":true,"shouldPadMedia":false,"hasCanvasAnimation":false},"a11y":{"tabindex":"-1"},"dividers":{"hasTopDivider":false,"hasBottomDivider":false},"translations":{"playLabel":"Play","pauseLabel":"Pause"}},"comp-jmhtolr4":{"crop":{"x":0,"y":0,"width":4032,"height":3024},"alt":"Roasting Hatch Chilis","width":4032,"height":3024,"uri":"577c92_a357298223394305bd0173cbed963358~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg","name":"20180914_134847.jpg","containerId":"comp-jmhtolr4","hasBgScrollEffect":"","bgEffectName":"","displayMode":"fill","link":{},"encoding":"AVIF","allowWebpAvifTransforms":true,"responsiveImageProps":{"fallbackSrc":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/577c92_a357298223394305bd0173cbed963358~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg/v1/fill/w_504,h_378,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/20180914_134847.jpg","srcset":"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/577c92_a357298223394305bd0173cbed963358~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg/v1/fill/w_504,h_378,al_c,q_80,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/20180914_134847.jpg 1x, https://static.wixstatic.com/media/577c92_a357298223394305bd0173cbed963358~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1008,h_756,al_c,q_85,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/20180914_134847.jpg 2x","css":{"container":{"position":"relative"},"img":{"width":504,"height":378,"objectFit":"cover"}}},"containerWidth":504,"containerHeight":378,"isInFirstFold":false,"onClickBehavior":"disabled","fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WPhoto","language":"en","compId":"comp-jmhtolr4","mainPageId":"qgy49","trackClicksAnalytics":false,"popupA11yExperimentEnabled":false,"translations":{"expandAriaLabel":"Expand image","zoomInButtonAriaLabel":"Zoom in"},"zoomedImageResponsiveOverride":{},"allowFullGIFTransformation":false},"comp-jmhtolsg":{"html":"<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">The Hatch chili&#39;s we get are mostly mild but flavorful after roasting and taking the seeds out so there&#39;s little fear of this sandwich being too spicy. Taste one and if you&#39;d like to add some kick to it you could add a few drops of hot sauce for sure, or not...</span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Bacon Cooking Tips:</span></span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">I recently bought a spectacular thick cut apple wood smoked bacon specifically for making sandwiches. </span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\">&nbsp;</h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">When I worked in restaurants we would bake copious&nbsp;amounts of bacon in the oven on baking sheets at 400 degrees for about 40 minutes to get the most perfectly precooked bacon for burgers, salads and&nbsp;sandwiches.</span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\">&nbsp;</h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">I cooked up my package this way and after cooling it on paper towels, stored it in a large plastic freezer bag in the refrigerator. If you can keep from eating it the minute it&#39;s done, this is a great way to prep for future recipes where&nbsp;cooking bacon just puts the whole recipe over the top in terms of prep time and mess.&nbsp;</span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">If you put a sheet of parchment paper under the bacon and wait for the grease to cool and harden (put it in the freezer or refrigerator&nbsp;to speed up this process) cleanup is amazingly easy. You may never cook bacon any other way again!</span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Link to <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"color:#2B6CA3;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><a href=\"http://www.theglasspantry.com/single-post/2018/09/20/sheet-pan-bacon\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Restaurant Style Sheet Pan Bacon</a></span></span> for the full blog.</span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></span></h5>\n\n<h5 class=\"font_5 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span class=\"wixGuard wixui-rich-text__text\">​</span></h5>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-jtajlknv":{"translations":{"title":"Widget Didn’t Load","text1":"Check your internet and refresh this page.","text2":"If that doesn’t work, contact us."}},"comp-jmhtolvc":{"html":"<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\" style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#1c1c1c;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-style:normal;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\"><span style=\"font-family:avenir-lt-w01_35-light1475496,sans-serif;\" class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Click through the gallery below for some tips and drool worthy photos on the making of these tasty BST Hatch Chili Sandwiches</span></span></span></span></span></p>","skin":"WRichTextNewSkin","isQaMode":false,"fullNameCompType":"wysiwyg.viewer.components.WRichText"},"comp-lo1v07rn":{"meshProps":{"wedges":[],"rotatedComponents":[],"fixedComponents":[]},"fillLayers":{"containerId":"comp-lo1v07rn","hasBgFullscreenScrollEffect":false,"shouldRenderUnderlay":true,"shouldPadMedia":false,"hasCanvasAnimation":false},"a11y":{"tabindex":"-1"},"dividers":{"hasTopDivider":false,"hasBottomDivider":false},"translations":{"playLabel":"Play","pauseLabel":"Pause"}},"comp-jmhtolwr":{"translations":{"title":"Widget Didn’t Load","text1":"Check your int